# ECC → SDD Skill Import Plan

Spec: ImportPlan
Purpose:
  Define the plan to import high-value ECC skills into the SDD system,
  bridging ECC's 281 skills with SDD's skill registry and chain graph.

Owns: evolution/import-plan.sdd

Source:
  ECC repository: https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC
  Total skills: 281
  High-relevance skills: ~20 (score >= 80%)
  Total agents: 67
  Total commands: 94

ImportPriority:
  P0_CRITICAL:
    description: Must-have for SDD chain execution
    criteria:
      - Directly maps to SDD chain arms (P1, D1, S1, C1, R1, DEP1)
      - Used in every project
      - No SDD equivalent exists
    skills:
      - tdd-workflow         → C1 (code) - test-first cycle
      - security-review      → R1 (review) - OWASP audit
      - build-error-resolver → C1 (code) - build fixes
      - code-architect       → D1 (docs) - architecture blueprints
      - refactor-clean       → C1 (code) - dead code removal
      - bdd-verification     → D1/S1 - behavior-driven specs

  P1_HIGH:
    description: High value, project-enables skills
    criteria:
      - Maps to specific SDD phases
      - 70%+ relevance to SDD workflows
      - Well-maintained ECC skills
    skills:
      - django-tdd           → C1 - Django test-first
      - django-security      → R1 - Django security audit
      - golang-patterns      → S1/C1 - Go conventions
      - typescript-patterns  → S1/C1 - TS conventions
      - react-patterns       → S1/C1 - React patterns
      - nextjs-patterns      → S1/C1 - Next.js patterns
      - python-patterns      → S1/C1 - Python conventions
      - database-reviewer    → R1 - DB query/schema review
      - security-scan        → R1 - AgentShield integration
      - code-review          → R1 - general code review

  P2_MEDIUM:
    description: Language-specific or niche skills
    criteria:
      - 50-70% relevance
      - Useful for specific stacks
    skills:
      - rust-patterns        → S1 - Rust conventions
      - go-reviewer          → R1 - Go-specific review
      - rust-reviewer        → R1 - Rust-specific review
      - java-reviewer        → R1 - Java-specific review
      - kotlin-reviewer      → R1 - Kotlin/Android review
      - cpp-reviewer         → R1 - C++ review
      - django-patterns      → S1 - Django architecture
      - go-build-resolver    → C1 - Go build fixes
      - java-build-resolver  → C1 - Java build fixes
      - flutter-reviewer     → R1 - Flutter/Dart review

  P3_LOW:
    description: Specialty or experimental skills
    criteria:
      - < 50% relevance to core
      - Highly specialized domains
    skills:
      - healthcare-reviewer  → R1 - healthcare compliance
      - homelab-architect    → D1 - home lab planning
      - marketing-agent      → D1/P1 - content planning
      - gan-planner          → D1 - GAN workflow planning
      - network-architect    → D1 - network design

ImportStrategy:
  phase_1:
    description: Import P0 critical skills
    target: .sdd/skills/
    format: Convert ECC Markdown SKILL.md → SDD .sdd spec files
    mapping:
      purpose: Use ECC skill "description" as SDD purpose
      steps: Use ECC skill "steps" as SDD execution
      constraints: Use ECC skill "constraints" as SDD rules
      output: Use ECC skill "expected output" as SDD output format

  phase_2:
    description: Import P1 high-value skills
    target: .sdd/skills/{domain}/
    format: Same conversion as phase 1
    additional:
      - Create domain directories (django/, go/, react/)
      - Link to existing SDD chain arms
      - Add to INDEX.sdd navigation

  phase_3:
    description: Import P2 medium-value skills
    target: .sdd/skills/{domain}/
    format: Same as above
    note: Language-specific reviewers map to @agent.reviewer

  phase_4:
    description: Document P3 low-value skills as references
    action: Create cross-reference entries in .sdd/references/sdd/
    note: Do not import full skill files — just reference links

AgentImport:
  target: .sdd/agent/ecc-bridge.sdd
  mapping:
    ECC agents → SDD @agent.* roles
    67 agents → 14 SDD roles + 23 specialty roles
    Store agent prompts as .sdd/agent/prompts/ (human-readable)

CommandImport:
  target: .claude/commands/
  existing: 14 SDD commands already exist
  new: Import ECC slash commands as .claude/commands/ entries
  mapping:
    /ecc:plan → /sdd-plan (alias to sdd.md)
    /code-review → extend existing review
    /security-scan → add to R1 review arm
    /build-fix → add to C1 code arm

RiskMitigation:
  - Each imported skill retains original ECC attribution
  - Import only skills with MIT license (ECC is MIT)
  - Validate skill structure before import
  - Create cross-references, not duplicates
  - Mark imported skills with @import.source = @ecc

Validation:
  - All imported .sdd files pass unit tests
  - Cross-references resolve correctly
  - No duplicate skills created
  - Chain graph updated with new skill references

State: +